    <h1 id="meet-the-team" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#meet-the-team">#</a> Meet the Team</h1>
<p>The people behind MarkoPass. We’re a diverse team of developers, designers, and documentation enthusiasts passionate about making the web faster.</p>
<h2 id="core-team" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#core-team">#</a> Core Team</h2>
<h3 id="patrick-(patrick)" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#patrick-(patrick)">#</a> Patrick (Patrick)</h3>
<p><strong>Founder &amp; Lead Developer</strong></p>
<p>Patrick is the creator of MarkoPress and a core contributor to Marko.js. With 15+ years of web development experience, he’s passionate about building fast, accessible websites.</p>
<p>📍 San Francisco, CA
🐦 <a href="https://twitter.com/patrick">@patrick</a>
🐙 <a href="https://github.com/patrick">github.com/patrick</a>
🔗 <a href="https://patrick.dev">patrick.dev</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p>“I built MarkoPress to solve my own frustrations with slow build times and complex setups. Every site should be fast by default.”</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<h3 id="sarah-chen" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#sarah-chen">#</a> Sarah Chen</h3>
<p><strong>Core Developer</strong></p>
<p>Sarah is a full-stack developer specializing in static site generators and build tools. She leads the plugin system development and maintains the core architecture.</p>
<p>📍 Seattle, WA
🐦 <a href="https://twitter.com/sarahcodes">@sarahcodes</a>
🐙 <a href="https://github.com/sarahcodes">github.com/sarahcodes</a>
🔗 <a href="https://sarahcodes.dev">sarahcodes.dev</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Great developer tools should be invisible. MarkoPress just works, so you can focus on creating content.”</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<h3 id="michael-rodriguez" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#michael-rodriguez">#</a> Michael Rodriguez</h3>
<p><strong>Documentation &amp; Community</strong></p>
<p>Michael ensures MarkoPress is well-documented and welcoming to everyone. He writes the guides, manages the community, and helps new users get started.</p>
<p>📍 Austin, TX
🐦 <a href="https://twitter.com/mikedocs">@mikedocs</a>
🐙 <a href="https://github.com/mikedocs">github.com/mikedocs</a>
🔗 <a href="https://mikedocs.dev">mikedocs.dev</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Documentation isn’t an afterthought—it’s the product. We strive to make every feature easy to understand and use.”</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<h3 id="emily-johnson" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#emily-johnson">#</a> Emily Johnson</h3>
<p><strong>Design &amp; UX</strong></p>
<p>Emily crafts the beautiful themes and intuitive user experience of MarkoPress. She believes great design should be accessible to everyone, not just design experts.</p>
<p>📍 New York, NY
🐦 <a href="https://twitter.com/emilydesigns">@emilydesigns</a>
🐙 <a href="https://github.com/emilydesigns">github.com/emilydesigns</a>
🔗 <a href="https://emilydesigns.co">emilydesigns.co</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Good design is invisible. Great design makes you feel like a pro, even if you’re just starting out.”</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
<h3 id="david-kim" tabindex="-1"><a class="header-anchor" href="#david-kim">#</a> David Kim</h3>
<p><strong>Performance &amp; Infrastructure</strong></p>
<p>David optimizes MarkoPress for speed and reliability. He works on build performance, caching strategies, and deployment integrations.</p>
<p>📍 Portland, OR
🐦 <a href="https://twitter.com/davidperf">@davidperf</a>
🐙 <a href="https://github.com/davidperf">github.com/davidperf</a>
🔗 <a href="https://davidperf.dev">davidperf.dev</a></p>
<blockquote>
<p>“Performance isn’t a feature—it’s a requirement. Every millisecond counts for user experience.”</p>
</blockquote>
<hr>
